From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:48:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 40/56] wayland: tell clients when the user goes idle with
 ext-idle-notify-v1

Implement ext_idle_notifier_v1 on top of the core idle monitor. Plain
notifications follow idle inhibitors like the session's own idle
handling; input notifications, from version 2, ignore them. Sandboxed
apps such as password managers that lock themselves after a while of
inactivity have no other way to learn the idle time. Each notification counts its
timeout from when it is created, as the protocol asks, rather than from
the last input before it.

Timeouts are at least a second, and at least ten seconds for sandboxed
clients, so no client can follow the rhythm of typing from when it goes
idle and resumes.

Upstream-Status: forwardable
